  <head><title>RedundantModifierCompactSource</title></head>
  <body>
    <section name="RedundantModifierCompactSource">
      <macro name="since"><param name="modulePath"
        value="src/main/java/com/puppycrawl/tools/checkstyle/checks/modifier/RedundantModifierCompactSourceCheck.java"/></macro>
      <subsection name="Description" id="RedundantModifierCompactSource_Description">
        <macro name="description"><param name="modulePath"
          value="src/main/java/com/puppycrawl/tools/checkstyle/checks/modifier/RedundantModifierCompactSourceCheck.java"/></macro>
        <p>
          The check reports <code>public</code>, <code>protected</code>, <code>final</code>,
          and <code>strictfp</code> modifiers on methods declared directly in compact source
          files.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <code>final</code> modifier is retained when it is required on a variable-arity,
          non-static, non-private instance method annotated with <code>@SafeVarargs</code>.
          An invalid fixed-arity use of <code>@SafeVarargs</code> does not prevent
          <code>final</code> from being reported.
        </p>
      </subsection>
      <subsection name="Examples" id="RedundantModifierCompactSource_Examples">
        <p id="Example1-config">To configure the check:</p>
        <macro name="example"><param name="path"
          value="resources-noncompilable/com/puppycrawl/tools/checkstyle/checks/modifier/redundantmodifiercompactsource/Example1.java"/><param name="type" value="config"/></macro>
        <p id="Example1-code">Example:</p>
        <macro name="example"><param name="path"
          value="resources-noncompilable/com/puppycrawl/tools/checkstyle/checks/modifier/redundantmodifiercompactsource/Example1.java"/><param name="type" value="code"/></macro>
      </subsection>
      <subsection name="Example of Usage" id="RedundantModifierCompactSource_Example_of_Usage">
